From {{m|en|torup|t=snapping turtle native to North America, especially the common snapping turtle (''Chelydra serpentina'')}}<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=torup|pos=n|id=76963077|date=December 2020|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|entry=torup|pos=n}}</ref> or from its {{glossary|etymon}} Virginia {{der|en|alg}} ''*tōrəp'' (“sea turtle”) + possibly [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ine|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming derivative or diminutive {{glossary|noun}}s}},<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=-ine|pos=suffix{{sup|4}}|noformat=1|id=94874|date=March 2021|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|entry=-ine|alt=-ine{{sup|4}}|pos=suf}}</ref> perhaps influenced by {{noncog|la|terra|t=dry land; soil; planet Earth}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=199512|date=June 2021|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> Compare {{cog|abe|tolba|t=turtle}}.

